From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Let the thread wait for its creator on emscripten

PxThreadImpl::start() spins until the new thread has stored its TID.
With emscripten, a thread started from the browser's main thread only
runs once a worker is free in the pthread pool, or else once the main
thread has returned to the event loop. The default CPU dispatcher starts
as many workers as there are cores, so with more cores than the pool has
workers the main thread spins forever and the page hangs.

Reverse the wait for emscripten, as the PhysX 4 copy did for
QTBUG-123888: start() marks the thread as started and releases it, and
the new thread waits for that before it runs. Nothing on emscripten
needs the TID, as the affinity calls do nothing there.

The 4.1 patch tested the macro with #ifdef, which PhysX always defines;
this one tests its value.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixThread.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixThread.cpp b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixThread.cpp
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixThread.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixThread.cpp
@@ -88,7 +88,13 @@ static void setTid(ThreadImpl& threadImpl)
 void* PxThreadStart(void* arg)
 {
 	ThreadImpl* impl = getThread(reinterpret_cast<PxThreadImpl*>(arg));
+#if PX_EMSCRIPTEN
+	// the parent does not wait for us, we wait for it, see start()
+	while(PxAtomicCompareExchange(&(impl->threadStarted), 1, 1) == 0)
+		sched_yield();
+#else
 	impl->state = ePxThreadStarted;
+#endif
 
 	// run setTid in thread's context
 	setTid(*impl);
@@ -163,6 +169,9 @@ void PxThreadImpl::start(uint32_t stackSize, PxRunnable* runnable)
 	}
 #endif
 
+#if PX_EMSCRIPTEN
+	getThread(this)->state = ePxThreadStarted;
+#endif
 	if(runnable && !getThread(this)->arg && !getThread(this)->fn)
 		getThread(this)->arg = runnable;
 
@@ -176,10 +185,17 @@ void PxThreadImpl::start(uint32_t stackSize, PxRunnable* runnable)
 	status = pthread_create(&getThread(this)->thread, &attr, PxThreadStart, this);
 	PX_ASSERT(!status);
 
+#if PX_EMSCRIPTEN
+	// A thread started from the browser's main thread only runs once the main thread returns
+	// to the event loop, unless a worker is free in the pthread pool, so waiting for it here
+	// can deadlock. Let the thread wait for us instead; nothing here needs its TID.
+	PxAtomicCompareExchange(&(getThread(this)->threadStarted), 1, 0);
+#else
 	// wait for thread to startup and write out TID
 	// otherwise TID dependent calls like setAffinity will fail.
 	while(PxAtomicCompareExchange(&(getThread(this)->threadStarted), 1, 1) == 0)
 		yield();
+#endif
 
 	// here we are sure that getThread(this)->state >= ePxThreadStarted
 
